Package: ovpnadm
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: rjeffmyers <rjeffmyers@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: bash (>= 5), openvpn (>= 2.5), easy-rsa (>= 3), dialog, netcat-openbsd, python3 (>= 3.9), sudo, openssl, iproute2, passwd, bsdextrautils | util-linux (<< 2.36)
Recommends: conntrack
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: OpenVPN server setup and user management with local Linux accounts
 ovpnadm sets up an OpenVPN server whose users log in with their Linux
 username and password (PAM, restricted to one group), optionally combined
 with a personal, expiring client certificate per person.
 .
 It provides a dialog menu and a command line to manage users, client
 certificates, connected sessions, logs and the client .ovpn profiles, and
 an optional self-service web page, reachable only through the VPN, where
 users renew their profile and change their password.
 .
 showvpn lists connected users and connection attempts. An add-on for
 iptables firewalls gives each user access to only their own hosts and ports.
